<h2>3. In-Depth Technical Engineering Details</h2>

<div class="card">
  <div class="card-title">1. BUG 02 — Lucky Bag Banner Size, Layering, and Duration</div>
  <div class="card-meta"><b>Target Files:</b> live_party_room_screen.dart, live_room_screen.dart, lucky_bag_sheet.dart</div>
  <div class="section-label">Root Cause Analysis:</div>
  <p>
    In Flutter's <code>Stack</code> widget, children placed earlier in the list are painted first, while later children are painted on top.
    <code>WorldLuckyBagBanner</code> was placed before the <code>SafeArea</code> containing the host avatar seat and mic grid. Consequently, the host seat circle was painted directly over the Lucky Bag banner, cutting through it.
    Additionally, the banner was hardcoded as a full-width container positioned at <code>top: padding.top + 60</code>, directly colliding with the stage header.
  </p>
  <div class="section-label">Engineering Solution:</div>
  <ul>
    <li>Moved <code>WorldLuckyBagBanner</code> to the very end of the root <code>Stack</code>, ensuring it occupies the topmost z-index foreground layer.</li>
    <li>Set <code>top: MediaQuery.padding.top + 8</code>, positioning the banner cleanly in the top-center above the room header and mic stage.</li>
    <li>Redesigned container into a compact floating pill (width: <code>320–380px</code>, height: <code>~64px</code>) featuring a deep purple gradient, royal gold border (<code>#FFD54F</code>), ambient glow, top crown motif (👑), animated gift icon, sender info, and coin badge (<code>× 8888 🪙</code>).</li>
    <li>Integrated an automated 3.4-second display timer with smooth <code>0.3s</code> slide-down entrance and <code>0.3s</code> slide-up exit animations.</li>
  </ul>
</div>

<div class="card">
  <div class="card-title">2. BUG 1, BUG 8 &amp; PK Viewer Real-Time Synchronization</div>
  <div class="card-meta"><b>Target Files:</b> live_party_provider.dart, live_party_room_screen.dart, pk_match_screen.dart, pk_battle_screen.dart</div>
  <div class="section-label">Root Cause Analysis:</div>
  <p>
    When a PK match started, the host called local state methods without broadcasting socket events to the room. Viewers in the room never received notifications, and mid-match joiners saw no battle because <code>onPkActive</code> was not subscribed to.
    Furthermore, <code>PkBattleScreen</code> contained fallback code that automatically generated fake PK sessions with <code>DummyData.popularUsers</code>.
  </p>
  <div class="section-label">Engineering Solution:</div>
  <ul>
    <li>Subscribed <code>LivePartyProvider</code> to <code>_socketService.onPkActive</code> and <code>onPkStarted</code>. When viewers join or reconnect, the provider queries <code>PKRepository.getActiveMatchForRoom()</code> to restore the live match.</li>
    <li>Starting a battle now emits <code>pk:start</code> and <code>room:pk_started</code> containing match ID, room IDs, countdown, and participant metadata.</li>
    <li>Match completion emits <code>pk:end</code> and <code>room:pk_ended</code> to tear down the battle overlay across all connected clients simultaneously.</li>
    <li>Eliminated all <code>DummyData</code> fallbacks across PK setup and battle screens. Only genuine, verified online hosts can be invited or matched.</li>
  </ul>
</div>

<div class="card">
  <div class="card-title">3. BUG 2 &amp; BUG 7 — Guest Microphone Invitation Delivery</div>
  <div class="card-meta"><b>Target Files:</b> live_party_provider.dart, live_party_room_screen.dart, live_viewers_sheet.dart, micInvite.service.js</div>
  <div class="section-label">Root Cause Analysis:</div>
  <p>
    The backend emitted invitations to both room channels and private channels, but client-side target user ID comparison failed when IDs contained numerical strings or <code>user_</code> prefixes. Additionally, the invitation dialog listener was not bound to the active view controller.
  </p>
  <div class="section-label">Engineering Solution:</div>
  <ul>
    <li>Added comprehensive target ID normalization in <code>LivePartyProvider</code> matching string IDs, numeric IDs, and usernames.</li>
    <li>Ensured the backend emits to <code>user:${targetUserId}</code> and room channels.</li>
    <li>Implemented an invitation prompt in <code>live_party_room_screen.dart</code> showing the inviter name, room title, and target mic seat with Accept and Decline actions.</li>
    <li>Accepting validates microphone permissions, claims the mic seat, and establishes Agora RTC audio streaming.</li>
  </ul>
</div>

<div class="card">
  <div class="card-title">4. BUG 3 — Viewer Profile Opening from Viewer Sheet</div>
  <div class="card-meta"><b>Target Files:</b> user_profile_details_screen.dart, live_viewers_sheet.dart</div>
  <div class="section-label">Root Cause Analysis:</div>
  <p>
    When tapping a viewer in the viewer list, the viewer model was passed via <code>widget.user</code>. In <code>_loadUser()</code>, the app called <code>auth.getUserById(widget.userId)</code>. If the cache returned null, the code assigned <code>_user = user</code>, destroying the valid viewer object and displaying "User profile not found".
  </p>
  <div class="section-label">Engineering Solution:</div>
  <ul>
    <li>Updated <code>_loadUser()</code> with safe null-coalescing: <code>user ??= _user ?? widget.user;</code> and <code>_user = user ?? _user ?? widget.user;</code>.</li>
    <li>The profile details screen now renders the viewer's data immediately without error.</li>
  </ul>
</div>

<div class="card card-critical">
  <div class="card-title">5. Issue 24 — SVIP / Noble Privileges &amp; 1.8M Points Leaking to New Accounts</div>
  <div class="card-meta"><b>Target Files:</b> svip_provider.dart, live_gift_provider.dart, user_profile_details_screen.dart</div>
  <div class="section-label">Root Cause Analysis:</div>
  <p>
    A newly created account displayed SVIP 7 tags and SVIP 3 with 1.8M points.
    Three distinct defects caused this anomaly:
    1) <code>SVIPProvider</code> saved points in SharedPreferences using global keys (<code>svip_current_points_v1</code>) without user scoping, carrying over data from previous logins.
    2) <code>syncWithUserWealth()</code> was syncing regular gift-sending wealth XP into SVIP recharge points.
    3) <code>LiveGiftProvider</code> awarded 1 SVIP point per coin spent on regular room gifts.
    4) When viewing another user's profile, the tag section fell back to the viewer's own local SVIP level.
  </p>
  <div class="section-label">Engineering Solution:</div>
  <ul>
    <li>Scoped all SharedPreferences storage keys by user ID: <code>svip_points_$userId</code> and <code>svip_level_$userId</code>. Unauthenticated or newly registered accounts initialize with 0 points and 0 level.</li>
    <li>Disabled automatic wealth XP syncing to SVIP recharge points.</li>
    <li>Removed SVIP point accrual from regular gift sending; SVIP points are strictly earned via verified recharge coin payments.</li>
    <li>In <code>UserProfileDetailsScreen</code>, ensured profile tags and badge galleries reflect strictly the target profile's SVIP level, never falling back to the local viewer's status.</li>
  </ul>
</div>

<div class="card">
  <div class="card-title">6. Issue 23 — King Noble Asset Mappings</div>
  <div class="card-meta"><b>Target Files:</b> aristocracy_center_screen.dart, noble_badge_helper.dart</div>
  <div class="section-label">Root Cause Analysis:</div>
  <p>
    In the King Aristocracy tier preview, Emperor/Imperial assets were assigned to the entrance effect and chat bubble, and the sword artwork was placed in the identity badge slot.
  </p>
  <div class="section-label">Engineering Solution:</div>
  <ul>
    <li>Identity Badge: <code>assets/nobles/ZP-034_tier-6-king_badge.webp</code></li>
    <li>Activate Effect: <code>assets/nobles/ZP-035_tier-6-king_badge.webp</code></li>
    <li>Chat Bubble: <code>assets/nobles/ZP-036_tier-6-king_badge.webp</code> (512x212)</li>
    <li>Entrance Effect: <code>assets/nobles/ZP-037_tier-6-king_badge.webp</code></li>
    <li>Mic Wave: <code>assets/nobles/king_mic.webp</code> (sword artwork assigned correctly to mic wave)</li>
  </ul>
</div>

<div class="card">
  <div class="card-title">7. BUG 4 &amp; Issue 20 — Noble Colored Usernames and Imperial Animation</div>
  <div class="card-meta"><b>Target Files:</b> noble_badge_helper.dart, animated_live_comment_item.dart, multi_role_seat_grid.dart</div>
  <div class="section-label">Engineering Solution:</div>
  <ul>
    <li>Configured Marquis / Mercurius username to Crimson Red (<code>#EF5350</code>).</li>
    <li>Configured King username to Royal Gold (<code>#FFD54F</code>).</li>
    <li>Implemented <code>AnimatedImperialUsername</code> with rotating blue (<code>#29B6F6</code>, <code>#4FC3F7</code>) and gold (<code>#FFD54F</code>, <code>#FFE082</code>) mixed gradient animation in both live chat and stage mic seat labels.</li>
    <li>Replaced internal placeholder keys ("user_free_920253") in Aristocracy preview with authentic user nicknames.</li>
  </ul>
</div>

<div class="card">
  <div class="card-title">8. BUG 5 — Room Restart Session Expiry Prevention</div>
  <div class="card-meta"><b>Target Files:</b> api_client.dart, room_repository.dart</div>
  <div class="section-label">Root Cause Analysis:</div>
  <p>
    When closing and restarting rooms, transient connection resets triggered <code>ApiClient._performTokenRefresh()</code>. Its catch block was unconditionally executing <code>clearTokens()</code>, wiping authentication credentials from secure storage and forcing the user to log in again.
  </p>
  <div class="section-label">Engineering Solution:</div>
  <ul>
    <li>Removed <code>clearTokens()</code> invocation on non-401 transient network errors. User tokens remain secure in persistent storage and valid sessions resume without re-login.</li>
  </ul>
</div>

<div class="card">
  <div class="card-title">9. Issues 12 &amp; 14 — Profile Glory (Received Gifts) &amp; Honor Galleries</div>
  <div class="card-meta"><b>Target Files:</b> user.controller.js, user.routes.js, user_profile_details_screen.dart</div>
  <div class="section-label">Engineering Solution:</div>
  <ul>
    <li>Implemented <code>GET /v1/users/:id/received-gifts</code> querying <code>giftTransaction</code> (excluding self-sent gifts) and aggregating by gift type. Built a Received Gifts Gallery grid with thumbnails, quantities (<code>×N</code>), and coin totals.</li>
    <li>Implemented <code>GET /v1/users/:id/honor-assets</code> returning active inventory. Built a categorized Honor Gallery (Titles, Frames, Entry Effects, Vehicles, Bubbles) with real asset previews and expiry indicators.</li>
  </ul>
</div>

